Curriculum
At Godwin Primary School we follow the National Curriculum. We plan from this ensuring we plan for a curriculum that:
…has reading at its heart - so that every child leaves us as a fluent reader, readily able to access the next stage of their learning;
…develops children’s vocabulary and equips them with skills to reduce social disadvantage;
…is based on our Godwin values (see below), as well as our ethos of working together and nurture, to promote positive emotional and physical health;
…provides experiences and opportunities that broaden children’s cultural capital and support the mindset that they can achieve anything, in order to encourage ambition and academic aspiration.
If you require any further information about the curriculum please ask your class teacher or Miss Spooner or send an email to the office which will be forwarded on.
